# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# worktrees
.worktrees/

# MkDocs build output
site/

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/*
*/__pycache__/*

# data files
*.json
!testdata/goldendataset.json
!testdata/trained_physics_iter29.json
!testdata/roofline_goldendataset.json
!testdata/catalog/models/**/config.json
# Vendored upstream artifacts (testdata/blis). Committed deliberately and pinned to an
# upstream commit -- see testdata/blis/VENDORED.md. Enumerated rather than blanket-allowed
# so an accidentally-dropped corpus is a visible diff rather than an untracked file.
!testdata/blis/measurements/*.json
!testdata/blis/catalog/models/**/config.json
!hardware_config.json
!specs/**/*.json
!cmd/testdata/**/*.json
!sim/latency/testdata/**/*.json
data/
*.txt

# auto-fetched HuggingFace model configs (downloaded by --roofline)

# binaries
#
# Leading-slash anchored so each matches ONLY the binary built in the repository root. An
# unanchored `blis` matches any path COMPONENT of that name at any depth, which silently
# excluded the whole of testdata/blis (the vendored catalog, registry, scenarios and
# measurement corpora) from `git add` -- the tree was present on disk, the tests passed,
# and nothing was committed. `inference-sim` unanchored has the same hazard against any
# directory sharing this repository's own name.
/blis
/blis_iter*
/inference-sim

# archon-go pr-review --out
.archon/

# results
results/
largesweep/
*.zip

# Training data pipeline (large data files — keep .py and .md only)
training

# Hypothesis experiment output (generated, reproducible from run.sh)
hypotheses/*/output/
hypotheses/*.yaml
!examples/*.yaml
!defaults.yaml
!hypotheses/**/*.yaml

# MkDocs symlink (created at build time, not committed — see C3 in PR #440)
docs/contributing.md

# uv files
.python-version
uv.lock
.DS_Store
*.ipynb
*.pyc

analysis_results/
analysis_results_*/
baseline_reg/
results_old/
.inference-sim-env/
saturation_regimes.xlsx
traces.csv

prompts.md

.venv/
actions-runner/

# Convergence review state (session-local, not committed)
.claude/convergence-state/

# Claude Code worktrees (created by EnterWorktree tool, not committed)
.claude/worktrees/

# Superpowers specs/plans (agent-local, not committed)
docs/superpowers/

# Bob-Shell notes (session-local, not committed)
.bob/notes

# Agent instruction files (generated, not committed)
AGENTS.md
.worktrees/
*.bak

# External-repo sibling directories cloned alongside inference-sim
ServeGen/
aiconfigurator/
gateway-api-inference-extension/
llm-d-inference-payload-processor/
llm-d-inference-scheduler/
llm-d-kv-cache/
llm-d-pd-utils/
llm-d-routing-sidecar/
llm-d/
sarathi-serve/
vidur/
vllm/

# Plans
docs/plans/

# Nous campaign orchestration (experiment worktrees + state, not committed)
.nous-experiments/
.nous/

# compiled scoring binaries (built with `go run`/`go build`; never artefacts in git)
/kernelscore
/estimatorscore
/metricscore

# Compiled probe binaries built in the repo root by `go build ./cmd/...`.
/signedprobe
